5. Create a Shape class with a nested interface Drawable.

   Interface method:
   void draw();

   Implement Drawable in Circle and Rectangle classes.
-->Interface method:

void draw();

Implement Drawable in Circle and Rectangle classes.

class Shape {

    interface Drawable {
        void draw();
    }
}

class Circle implements Shape.Drawable {

    public void draw() {
        System.out.println("Drawing Circle");
    }
}

class Rectangle implements Shape.Drawable {

    public void draw() {
        System.out.println("Drawing Rectangle");
    }
}

public class Demo {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Shape.Drawable c = new Circle();
        Shape.Drawable r = new Rectangle();

        c.draw();
        r.draw();
    }
}







6. Create a multi-level inner class program.

   Outer → Inner → InnerInner

   Access all levels and print the variables.
-->Outer → Inner → InnerInner

Access all levels and print variables.

class Outer {

    int x = 10;

    class Inner {

        int y = 20;

        class InnerInner {

            int z = 30;

            void display() {

                System.out.println("x = " + x);
                System.out.println("y = " + y);
                System.out.println("z = " + z);
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Outer o = new Outer();
        Outer.Inner i = o.new Inner();
        Outer.Inner.InnerInner ii = i.new InnerInner();

        ii.display();
    }
}








7. Implement a Thread using an anonymous inner class inside a method of an outer class.
-->class Outer {

    void startThread() {

        Thread t = new Thread() {

            public void run() {

                for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
                    System.out.println("Thread : " + i);
                }
            }
        };

        t.start();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Outer obj = new Outer();
        obj.startThread();
    }
}
Interview Tip

Remember these definitions:

Nested Interface: An interface declared inside another class or interface.
Member Inner Class: A non-static class declared inside another class.
Static Nested Class: A static class declared inside another class.
Anonymous Inner Class: A class without a name, used for one-time implementation.
